    "body": "## Motivation\n\nThe fused k-pool decode, target-verify, and draft-extend metadata kernels are disabled on HIP even when the geometry is supported. Enable the existing kernels on HIP to avoid the separate metadata operations.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Accept HIP alongside CUDA in the platform eligibility check. Retain the geometry checks and the `SGLANG_EXPERIMENTAL_DSA_KPOOL_METADATA_FUSION` opt-out.\n- Register the existing target-verify replay regression for AMD MI35x CI.\n- Update the branch against main `7d9bc10493275a371989bd03a13147588005f136`.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nValidated commit `4458382cdfd1b749d409034e5c657233b3e493e2` on MI355X/gfx950, PyTorch `2.11.0+rocm7.2`, HIP `7.2.26015`, and Triton `3.7.0`:\n\n| Check | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| Direct decode/verify/draft-extend metadata matrix | 85/85 GPU cases passed |\n| Graph replays within that matrix | 170 passed |\n| Platform/geometry/flag dispatch combinations | 22/22 passed |\n| Registered verify replay regression | Passed, including three input updates/replays |\n\nThe direct matrix checks exact integer metadata against independent PyTorch references, guarded output buffers, strided inputs/outputs, variable and zero-length draft extension, and actual row offsets above 2^31 elements. It covers pool sizes 2/4/8/16/32/64 and selected batch, context-length, top-k, and speculative-width boundaries. Production kernel and dispatch sources are unchanged in the validation payload. The harness isolates package initialization/test utilities; it does not execute a full serving process.\n\nRegistered regression command on MI355X:\n\n```bash\npython test/registered/kernels/ops/attention/test_dsa_kpool_metadata_fusion.py\n```\n\nFull-model GSM8K has not been rerun in this quick validation. These are metadata correctness results, not a model-accuracy score.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNo verified end-to-end speed result is claimed in this update. A matched serving comparison remains pending; the original approximate decode-step timing is removed because its raw timing records and full configuration were not recovered.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format code: scoped Ruff lint/format, isort, codespell, syntax, and diff checks pass.\n- [x] Add regression coverage: register the replay test for AMD MI35x CI.\n- [x] Documentation: no new option or API; existing opt-out is retained.\n- [ ] Provide full-model accuracy and reproducible serving-speed results.\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style guidance.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39499214607](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39499214607)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39499214612](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39499214612)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39499214740](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39499214740)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->\n",
